  7.2 Extract | This script is run once 7.1 is finished and results exported as an asset. 
      It calculates/extracts five different bands. The idea is to detect the break dates (disturbance dates) and apply a given threshold (e.g. 10000) to only the 
      negative values of the NDFI magnitude change band.
      
  This method has not been automated -> Thus, there is still run to improve and automate the process by including the assets on an image collection rather than as separated images.
      Then we could use the same grid as to automate the process to extract the desired bands and/or apply any other operation (e.g. apply thresholds on the NDFI magnitude)

  - Parameters that can be changed:
      - aoi: area of interest
      - cg_scale: Defines the size of the tiles. The greater the size, the more time will take the task to process. 
      - tilelist: list of tiles that will be processed
      - start | end: Dates to create the Landsat image collection
      - daterange: Dates to define the CCD period over which the extraction will happen. Currently changes between 2021 and May 2024.
      - breakpoint variables contains a set of additional options (see in comments)
      - ndfiMag_gte10k: See gte threshold. It is currently set to identify a drop higher or equal than 10000.
      - mmu_p: number of connected pixels that will be removed (currently 8)

